				</ukm:Metadata><Primary><Body DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2002/16/body" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16/body" NumberOfProvisions="24" RestrictStartDate="2026-03-15"><Pblock DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2002/16/crossheading/aggregation" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16/crossheading/aggregation" NumberOfProvisions="1" id="crossheading-aggregation" RestrictStartDate="2005-12-05"><Title>Aggregation</Title><P1group ConfersPower="true" RestrictExtent="E+W+S" RestrictStartDate="2005-12-05"><Title> Income and capital of claimant, spouse <Abbreviation Expansion="Et cetera" xml:lang="la">etc</Abbreviation></Title><P1 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2002/16/section/5" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16/section/5" id="section-5"><Pnumber PuncAfter=""><CommentaryRef Ref="c4497471"/><CommentaryRef Ref="c4550591"/><CommentaryRef Ref="key-a8"/>5</Pnumber><P1para><Text>Where the claimant is a member of a  <Substitution ChangeId="key-a9" CommentaryRef="key-a9">couple</Substitution> , the income and capital of the other member of the couple shall, except in prescribed circumstances, be treated for the purposes of this Act as income and capital of the claimant.</Text></P1para></P1></P1group></Pblock></Body></Primary><Commentaries><Commentary id="c4497471" Type="I"><Para><Text>S. 5 partly in force; s. 5 not in force at Royal Assent, see s. 22(3); s. 5 in force for certain purposes at 2.7.2002 by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2002/1691" id="c00029" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2002" Number="1691">S.I. 2002/1691</Citation>, <CitationSubRef id="c00030" CitationRef="c00029" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2002/1691/article/2" SectionRef="article-2" Operative="true">art. 2</CitationSubRef></Text></Para></Commentary><Commentary id="c4550591" Type="C"><Para><Text>S. 5: power to apply conferred (prosp.) by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1992/4" id="c00032" Year="1992" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct" Number="4" Title="Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992">Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (c. 4)</Citation>, <CitationSubRef id="c00033" CitationRef="c00032" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1992/4/section/136A/3/a" Operative="true" SectionRef="section-136A-3-a">s. 136A(3)(a)</CitationSubRef> (as inserted (prosp.) by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16" id="c00034" Year="2002" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct" Number="16" Title="State Pension Credit Act 2002">State Pension Credit Act 2002 (c. 16)</Citation>, <CitationSubRef id="c00035" CitationRef="c00034" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16/section/14" SectionRef="section-14">ss. 14</CitationSubRef>, <CitationSubRef id="c00036" CitationRef="c00034" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16/section/22/3" SectionRef="section-22-3">22(3)</CitationSubRef>, <CitationSubRef id="c00037" CitationRef="c00034" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16/schedule/2/paragraph/3" Operative="true" SectionRef="schedule-2-paragraph-3">Sch. 2 para. 3</CitationSubRef>)</Text></Para></Commentary><Commentary id="key-a9" Type="F"><Para><Text>Words in <CitationSubRef id="c3u050wo3-00006" SectionRef="section-5" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2002/16/section/5">s. 5</CitationSubRef> substituted (5.12.2005) by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2004/33" id="c3u050wo3-00007" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct" Year="2004" Number="33" Title="Civil Partnership Act 2004">Civil Partnership Act 2004 (c. 33)</Citation>, <CitationSubRef id="c3u050wo3-00008" CitationRef="c3u050wo3-00007" SectionRef="section-263-8-d" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2004/33/section/263/8/d">s. 263(8)(d)</CitationSubRef>, <CitationSubRef id="c3u050wo3-00009" CitationRef="c3u050wo3-00007" SectionRef="schedule-24-paragraph-140" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2004/33/schedule/24/paragraph/140" Operative="true">Sch. 24 para. 140</CitationSubRef>; <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2005/3175" id="c3u050wo3-00010" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2005" Number="3175" Title="The Civil Partnership Act 2004 (Commencement No. 2) Order 2005">S.I. 2005/3175</Citation>, <CitationSubRef id="c3u050wo3-00011" CitationRef="c3u050wo3-00010" SectionRef="article-2-1" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2005/3175/article/2/1">art. 2(1)</CitationSubRef>, <CitationSubRef id="c3u050wo3-00012" CitationRef="c3u050wo3-00010" SectionRef="schedule-1" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2005/3175/schedule/1">Sch. 1</CitationSubRef></Text></Para></Commentary><Commentary id="key-a8" Type="I"><Para><Text>S. 5 in force at 6.10.2003 in so far as not already in force  by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2003/1766" id="c3ru6z6v3-00100" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2003" Number="1766" Title="The State Pension Credit Act 2002 (Commencement No.5) and Appointed Day Order 2003">S.I. 2003/1766</Citation>, <CitationSubRef id="c3ru6z6v3-00101" CitationRef="c3ru6z6v3-00100" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2003/1766/article/2/a" SectionRef="article-2-a" Operative="true">art. 2(a)</CitationSubRef></Text></Para></Commentary></Commentaries></Legislation>